# bind-config.map — git-tracked config paths that are BIND-MOUNTED into a service,
# and the service that must be RESTARTED when they change.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# `docker compose up -d` only recreates a container when the COMPOSE DEFINITION
# changes. A bind-mounted file changing is invisible to it: compose prints
# "Running" and moves on, the container keeps its old config, and nothing says so.
#
# Verified on the box 2026-08-16: after `git pull` brought a new
# ha/packages/*.yaml, `docker compose up -d home-assistant` reported "Running"
# and HA's uptime was unchanged — the new config was NOT loaded.
#
# That is the same silent-failure shape SPEC.md already warns about three times
# (`ports:` under host networking, `ports:` under `network_mode: service:`, and
# the missing-bind-path trap). This file plus scripts/deploy.sh is the fix.
#
# FORMAT: <repo-relative path prefix> <compose service>
# Whitespace-separated. Lines starting with # and blank lines ignored.
#
# ADDING A BIND MOUNT? Add a row here. scripts/verify.sh FAILS if compose declares
# a `./` bind with no row, so this cannot silently fall out of date.

cloudflared/              cloudflared
ha/packages/              home-assistant
media/gerbera/            gerbera
